560	// THE `agentic` FIELD IS RETIRED (#768 Phase 5), and its successor is `applyStage`
561	// below. A record used to carry `agentic: { model, instructions }` — member-side
562	// adaptation no script could do — and baselining's code-work read it to decide whether
563	// a pending note needed an agent stage, holding the member's stamp until one ran.
564	//
565	// What the successor drops is the MODEL knob. Which model runs a session is the
566	// scheduler's answer (packs/claudinite-tasks/model-map.mjs, off the task declaration), and
567	// a record reaching around it to name its own was a second authority over the same
568	// fact. What a record legitimately knows is narrower and is all `applyStage` asks
569	// for: whether its change needs a session at all, and what that session must do.
570	//
571	// The field is not merely ignored, it is REJECTED. An ignored field on a record
572	// someone writes in good faith is work that silently never happens; the whole reason
573	// the note existed was that skipping such work quietly is a correctness risk (#405).
574	// Failing at load turns a stale or hopeful note into an error with a fix attached.
575	export function assertNoAgenticNote(m) {
576	  if (m?.agentic === undefined || m?.agentic === null) return;
577	  throw new Error(`migration ${m.id}: the "agentic" field was retired in #768 Phase 5 and is no longer run. `
