582	// THE `applyStage` FIELD: this record's change needs a session on the member.
583	//
584	// It exists because the alternative was worse. The pack flow used to decide the
585	// apply stage from its VERSION PLAN — "any pack version moved" — which is a fact
586	// about the CANON, while the stage exists for a fact about the MEMBER: the pack's
587	// new rules met content the canon has never seen. Since a record can only reach an
588	// up-to-date member if its pack's manifest version bumps, and every bump fired the
589	// stage, a purely mechanical migration — a regex rewrite, a declaration seed — could
590	// not be shipped without spending an agent session on every member in the fleet
591	// (#798). The record's author knows which of the two kinds they wrote; a version
592	// number never can.
593	//
594	// SHAPE, VALIDATED AT LOAD for the same reason the retired field is rejected there:
595	// a record whose declaration is malformed must fail where it is written, not go
